        "original_id": "76c284bd-999c-5687-b91d-dd4d36a55fa5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Munich, Germany, Netherlands\n- Companies: Löwenbräu, Anheuser-Busch InBev\n- Organizations: German Nazi government, Britain\n- People: Georg Elser, Adolf Hitler\n- Events: Venlo Incident, failed assassination attempt, Germany's invasion of the Netherlands\n- Buildings: Bürgerbräukeller\n\nFacts:\n- The Bürgerbräukeller was a large beer hall in Munich, Germany.\n- Löwenbräu is a brewery in Munich owned by Anheuser-Busch InBev.\n- On 8 November 1939, Georg Elser carried out a failed assassination attempt on German Chancellor Adolf Hitler at the Bürgerbräukeller in Munich, Germany.\n- The German Nazi government later used the Venlo Incident to link Britain to Georg Elser's failed assassination attempt.\n- The German Nazi government also used the Venlo Incident to help justify Germany's invasion of the neutral Netherlands on 10 May 1940.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
